{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HimA7tbd1AoBwAKQbgiVeS","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search through the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\\\n\\\\nThe final exact name of the new StreamsConfig property that lets applications opt into headers-aware DSL stores is: **`dsl.store.format`**\\\\n\\\\nThis property was originally proposed as `dsl.store.type`, but the name was changed to `dsl.store.format` based on reviewer feedback during the KIP-1285 voting phase. The change was made to provide a clearer distinction from the existing `dsl.store.suppliers.class` configuration property, which could have caused ambiguity if both used similar naming.\\\\n\\\\n**Citations:**\\\\n- `/store/kips-and-discussions.md` (line 856): \\\\\\\"Config naming: dsl.store.format (vs type) - clearer distinction from dsl.store.suppliers.class\\\\\\\"\\\\n- `/store/window-38-summary.md` (line 187): \\\\\\\"Feedback on config naming: dsl.store.type vs dsl.store.format\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis is part of **KIP-1285: DSL Opt-in Support for Header-Aware State Stores**, which builds on KIP-1271's headers-aware state store infrastructure to provide DSL-level configuration for applications to enable header-aware stores.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"kips-and-discussions.md\\\",\\\"window-38-summary.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests.md\\\",\\\"window-34-summary.md\\\",\\\"window-40-summary.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":59.69,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":661827,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":51816,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1890877,\\\"input_tokens\\\":138,\\\"output_tokens\\\":3827}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3c01f60-1320-45d9-a0a0-557dc6e63d7d","uuid":"62adcd44-f3b5-464a-8a15-720253d4172d","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:07:45.533Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search through the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\\\n\\\\nThe final exact name of the new StreamsConfig property that lets applications opt into headers-aware DSL stores is: **`dsl.store.format`**\\\\n\\\\nThis property was originally proposed as `dsl.store.type`, but the name was changed to `dsl.store.format` based on reviewer feedback during the KIP-1285 voting phase. The change was made to provide a clearer distinction from the existing `dsl.store.suppliers.class` configuration property, which could have caused ambiguity if both used similar naming.\\\\n\\\\n**Citations:**\\\\n- `/store/kips-and-discussions.md` (line 856): \\\\\\\"Config naming: dsl.store.format (vs type) - clearer distinction from dsl.store.suppliers.class\\\\\\\"\\\\n- `/store/window-38-summary.md` (line 187): \\\\\\\"Feedback on config naming: dsl.store.type vs dsl.store.format\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis is part of **KIP-1285: DSL Opt-in Support for Header-Aware State Stores**, which builds on KIP-1271's headers-aware state store infrastructure to provide DSL-level configuration for applications to enable header-aware stores.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"kips-and-discussions.md\\\",\\\"window-38-summary.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests.md\\\",\\\"window-34-summary.md\\\",\\\"window-40-summary.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":59.69,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":661827,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":51816,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1890877,\\\"input_tokens\\\":138,\\\"output_tokens\\\":3827}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on my search through the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\n\\nThe final exact name of the new StreamsConfig property that lets applications opt into headers-aware DSL stores is: **`dsl.store.format`**\\n\\nThis property was originally proposed as `dsl.store.type`, but the name was changed to `dsl.store.format` based on reviewer feedback during the KIP-1285 voting phase. The change was made to provide a clearer dis